dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.drawing.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.drawing
start body
framing record

# drawing wave: REAL binary op frame, replacing the old whole-enum `serde_json::to_vec` shortcut
# (`🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioDrawingMutation` is a genuine
# data-carrying enum whose variants embed nested `DrawLayer`/`DrawNode`/`PathSegment`/
# `SemioDrawingSnapshot` payloads — `DrawNode` is additionally RECURSIVE — no `dsl::DslField` impl
# exists for these hand-rolled tagged enums (per this subset's own `📸️snapshot`/`🔺️diff`
# convention), so the generic derive-based `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout
# doesn't apply. Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the
# `SemioDrawingMutation` variant ordinal, `🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/
# `variant_ordinal`, same 0-17 ordering as `parse_semio_drawing_mutation`'s keyword match) as two
# REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own `key=value ...` argument payload as one opaque trailing
# `bytes` chain — the same honest boundary the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`
# uses (`protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, per the recipe's gap table).
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
